# Line endings.
#
# Text files are normalised to LF in the repository and checked out however the
# platform prefers — except the ones below, where CRLF is a bug rather than a
# preference.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts MUST be LF, on every platform. A CRLF shebang fails with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", and tools/build_bundle.py copies install.sh
# out of the working tree into the Linux bundle — so a bundle built on a
# Windows checkout would ship a script that cannot run.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.command   text eol=lf

# Inno Setup and Windows batch want CRLF.
*.iss       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch these.
#
# *.pdf earns its place the hard way: docs/ now carries the installation guide,
# and Git classified it as *text* because the file happens to hold no NUL byte
# near the start. Under `* text=auto` above, a fresh clone on Windows would
# have rewritten every LF in it to CRLF and produced a PDF no reader opens.
*.png       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.ico       binary
*.icns      binary
*.zip       binary
*.tar.gz    binary
*.dmg       binary
*.exe       binary
